w = np.array([2.0, -0.5, 30.0])
print((X @ w + 4.0).shape)
--- options
* (200,)
(200, 1)
(3,)
(200, 3)
--- explain
`(200, 3) @ (3,)` contracts the shared dimension of length 3 and leaves one number per row: a 1-D array of shape `(200,)`. Adding the scalar bias doesn''t change the shape.
```

