```python exercise id=neuron-gradient title="Gradient of a single sigmoid neuron"
# TODO: `grad_w(x, w, t)` should return dL/dw for the loss L = (sigmoid(w * x) - t) ** 2,
# where sigmoid(z) = 1 / (1 + exp(-z)). Use the chain rule.
